Flow Inference is an independently implemented research inference engine.
Its Python runtime does not import or launch vLLM or SGLang.

Design references include vLLM's paged KV and continuous scheduling, SGLang's
prefix reuse and scheduling separation, and online softmax attention literature.
Source review versions: vLLM v0.31.0, SGLang v0.5.21. See docs/SOURCES.md.
This repository does not vendor their source or model weights.

PyTorch, Transformers, Triton, FastAPI, safetensors and other dependencies retain
their own licenses. Referenced model licenses apply separately to downloaded
checkpoints. The MIT license here grants no rights to those weights.

No affiliation with or endorsement by upstream teams is implied. This project
does not claim global novelty for paging, prefix reuse, prompt lookup or fusion.
